#!/bin/bash
# Getting-around guide for students using the lab PC (Hyprland). Matches ~/.config/hypr/keybinds.lua.
set -euo pipefail

cat << 'EOF'
==========================================================
   Lab PC Help: getting around Hyprland
==========================================================

This computer uses Hyprland, a "tiling" window manager. There is no start
menu, taskbar or desktop icons. New windows tile next to each other
automatically, and you do most things with the keyboard.

SUPER is the Windows key (the one with the logo, next to Alt).

Stuck? Press SUPER + /  to search every shortcut.
       Run   help-lab-pc  in a terminal to see this page again.

----------------------------------------------------------
 Opening programs
----------------------------------------------------------
    SUPER + R               app launcher: start typing a name, then Enter
    SUPER + T               new terminal (kitty)
    SUPER + B               web browser (Firefox)
    SUPER + E               volume mixer

  File explorer (Dolphin):
    1. Press SUPER + R
    2. Type  dolphin
    3. Press Enter
    Or from a terminal:  dolphin &     (opens in the current folder: dolphin . &)

  Terminal file manager (faster once you know it):
    yazi                    arrow keys / h j k l to move, q to quit

----------------------------------------------------------
 Windows
----------------------------------------------------------
    SUPER + Q               close the window
    SUPER + Z               force-kill a frozen window
    ALT + h / j / k / l     focus the window left / down / up / right
    SUPER + ALT + h/j/k/l   swap the window with its neighbour
    SUPER + CTRL + h/j/k/l  resize the window
    SUPER + V               float / unfloat (a floating window can sit on top)
    ALT + left-drag         move a window with the mouse
    ALT + right-drag        resize a window with the mouse

  Clicking a window also focuses it.

----------------------------------------------------------
 Workspaces (the numbered circles, top left)
----------------------------------------------------------
  Workspaces are separate screens. Use them to keep things apart, for
  example code on 1, browser on 2, data and plots on 3.

    Click a number          go to that workspace
    SUPER + 1 ... 9, 0      go to workspace 1 ... 10
    SUPER + A S D F G H J K go to workspace 1 ... 8 (home row)
    SUPER + SHIFT + number  move the current window to that workspace
                            (SUPER + SHIFT + A S D F ... works too)

  The white circle is where you are. Icons next to a number show what is
  open there; hover over it to see the window titles.

----------------------------------------------------------
 The top bar
----------------------------------------------------------
  Right side, click to open:
    Vol     audio settings           Wifi    network settings
    BT      Bluetooth devices        CPU/GPU system monitor (btop, q quits)
  Scroll on Vol to change the volume.

----------------------------------------------------------
 Copy and paste
----------------------------------------------------------
    CTRL + C / CTRL + V          copy / paste in normal apps
    CTRL + SHIFT + C / V         copy / paste in the terminal
                                 (CTRL + C in a terminal stops the running program)

----------------------------------------------------------
 Leaving the computer
----------------------------------------------------------
    SUPER + X               lock the screen (unlock with the account password)
  Please save your work and close your windows when you are done.

==========================================================
EOF
